# Atomic Components & File Size Limits

Write small, focused components. Each file should do one thing well.

## Line Count Targets

| Range | Action |
|-------|--------|
| **200–300 lines** | Ideal target for most components, hooks, and page files |
| **301–350 lines** | Acceptable only with a brief comment explaining why (e.g. tightly coupled layout) |
| **350+ lines** | Must split before finishing the task — no exceptions without explicit user approval |

When creating or editing a file, check its length. If it will exceed **300 lines**, stop and refactor first.

## How to Split

Extract into the feature's `hooks/` and `components/` folders (see the feature-folder-structure rule):

- **UI pieces** → `components/` (`LandingHeroIntro.tsx`, `OrderDetailsStatCard.tsx`)
- **Feature-local hooks** → `hooks/useXxx.ts` (state, effects, data fetching)
- **Constants & types** → feature-root `constants.ts`, `types.ts`
- **Pure helpers** → feature-root `utils.ts`, `motion.ts`
- **Orchestrator** → thin parent at the feature root that composes children (≤ 100 lines when possible)

## Component Rules

- One primary export per file; name the file after that export
- Move inline subcomponents out once they exceed ~40 lines or are reused
- Keep business logic in hooks/utils, not in JSX-heavy files
- Prefer composition over large prop-drilling monoliths

## Examples

```
❌ BAD — 500-line LandingHeroPanelSection.tsx with 8 inline components

✅ GOOD
app/features/landing/
  LandingHeroPanelSection.tsx
  constants.ts
  motion.ts
  hooks/
    useLandingHeroSignUpReveal.ts
  components/
    LandingHeroIntro.tsx
    LandingHowItWorksSection.tsx
```

## Allowed Exceptions (still prefer splitting)

- Auto-generated files (`.gen.ts`, codegen output)
- Large static config/data maps with no logic
- Third-party vendored or copied code

For any other exception over 300 lines, ask the user before leaving the file unsplit.
